rem Palindromic Sums
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=125
rem Sum the palindromes below a limit
rem that are sums of two or more
rem consecutive squares

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option Limit integer = 100000000

rem Prefix sums P of the squares give a
rem run of L squares from i as
rem P[i + L] - P[i]. Take every start
rem and every length at once.
Top = Limit isqrt
N = 1 to Top array
Pre = N * N scan + with 0 copy
Most = (Pre less Limit) count
Cols = Most - 1
Cells = Top * Cols
St = (0 till Top array) reshape Top 1
Ln = (2 to Most array) reshape 1 Cols
End = St + Ln
Fit = End at most Top
At = (End Top min) reshape Cells
Hi = (Pre At) reshape Top Cols
Sv = 0 till Top array
Lo = (Pre Sv) reshape Top 1
Run = Hi - Lo
Ok = Fit and Run less Limit
Cand = Run filter Ok array unique
Txt = Cand text rank 0
Pal = Txt equal (Txt reverse rank 0)
Answer = Cand filter Pal sum
Answer print
